<!--
  The themed-icon variant, for Android 13+ where the launcher discards every colour and tints the
  whole mark one flat shade.

  ## Why this is drawn differently rather than recoloured

  It cannot be the colour foreground with the colours removed. There the pulse is green on a solid
  white body; strip the colour and it becomes the tint drawn on the tint - a blank slab with the whole
  point of the icon gone. So the body is an outline here and the pulse sits in the empty middle, where
  it reads against transparency instead of against fill.

  ## What this variant is not

  Ideally the silhouette would match the colour version exactly, with the pulse punched out of a solid
  body as genuine transparency. A VectorDrawable can only do that by expressing the pulse as a closed
  outline inside an evenOdd path, which means converting a stroked zigzag into a polygon by hand -
  offsetting each vertex along its bisector, and clamping the mitre where the turns are sharp or the
  joints spike. That is a real piece of geometry and it is not written yet, so this is an outline
  instead: honest, legible, and visibly a sibling rather than a twin.

  Geometry: body inset to 37..71 x 26..82 with a 8-wide stroke, which straddles the path and puts the
  outer edge back at 33..75 - the same footprint as the colour version, reaching 33.9 from centre.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <path
        android:strokeColor="#FAFAFA"
        android:strokeWidth="8"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:pathData="M45,26h18a8,8 0 0,1 8,8v40a8,8 0 0,1 -8,8h-18a8,8 0 0,1 -8,-8V34a8,8 0 0,1 8,-8z" />

    <path
        android:strokeColor="#FAFAFA"
        android:strokeWidth="7"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeLineJoin="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:pathData="M42,54h4l4,-9l5,18l4,-9h5" />
</vector>
